<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oda Nobutada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1557">1557</a>–<a href="/years/1582">1582</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oda Nobutada was the eldest son and heir of the Japanese warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>. He received headship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-clan">Oda clan</a> in the mid-1570s and led the campaign that destroyed the Takeda in 1582. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akechi-mitsuhide">Akechi Mitsuhide</a> attacked Nobunaga at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honno-ji">Honnō-ji</a> in June 1582, Nobutada was trapped at Nijō in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> and took his own life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oda-nobutada.jpg" alt="Oda Nobutada" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 投稿者がファイル作成 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oda_Nobutada3_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
